  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jordan - Support for Renewable Energy Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed Japan Climate Change Initiative Grant of about $1.0 million would support the following activities: 1.  Wind and solar energy resource assessment to develop wind and solar energy atlasses and information database. 2.  Legal framework for renewable energy development. 3.  Energy audit in medium scale industries. 4.  Geothermal and energy development. 5.  Feasibility study for commercial size windfarm projects. 10/23/03.  Govt of Japan approved today the Grant of US$1.0 million. 01/18/04.  The Grant Agreement was counter-signed by the Jordanian Government. 7/20/04.  Consultants are in the process of being recruited to undertake the various activities described above.  FY05 BB allocation: $10K for TF supervision.</narrative>
  </description>
